Reviewed `src/blog/people/drafts/Alexandr-Wang.md` and appended a `FRESH EYES REVIEW` block at the bottom. No body edits.

**The two biggest flags:**

1. **The labelers are missing.** The draft's central thesis is that Wang industrialized other people's judgment — there's a pull quote celebrating it — but the people inside that machinery never appear. Scale's Remotasks arm drew a [Washington Post investigation](https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2023/08/28/scale-ai-remotasks-philippines-artificial-intelligence/) over Philippine workers who often weren't paid, and cut off Kenyan, Nigerian and Pakistani labelers in March 2024 with work outstanding. The research file already flagged it ("an army of clickworkers"); the draft skipped it. As written, "human judgment goes in, labeled signal comes out" reads as admiring — and it's the exact sentence a critic would use against him.

2. **The piece asks "can the composite lead the specialists?" then withholds the evidence.** Named researchers left Meta's AI org on his watch (all four are in the research file, none in the draft), and Meta reportedly paid $100M-plus packages to poach ~20 researchers from OpenAI, DeepMind and Anthropic — with Wang publicly [rejecting](https://www.shopifreaks.com/meta-ai-chief-alexandr-wang-denies-superintelligence-lab-recruits-are-money-motivated-despite-reported-100m-offers/) the idea they were money-motivated as "an incorrect assumption." That's the best unused artifact in the record for a Type 3 read: the man who built a business ranking people insisting his own hires can't be read off their price tag.

Also flagged: the "Scale is cooked" quote arrives with the charge never stated ([OpenAI wound down](https://techcrunch.com/2025/06/18/openai-drops-scale-ai-as-a-data-provider-following-meta-deal), Google moved to cut ties, [200 laid off](https://www.cnbc.com/2025/07/16/scale-ai-cuts-14percent-of-workforce-after-meta-investment-hiring-of-wang.html)), the benchmark table spends its space on recap, and the Type 5 counter-argument runs twice in nearly the same words. Preserved as working: the Disney World spine, the all-hands interior beat, the Alex Ren / LeCun pairing, and the contributor-tier close.
